{
  // Visit https://aka.ms/tsconfig to read more about this file
  "compilerOptions": {
    // File Layout
    // "rootDir": "./src",
    // "outDir": "./dist",
    // Environment Settings
    // See also https://aka.ms/tsconfig/module
    "module": "esnext",
    "target": "es2018",
    "types": [
      "vitest/globals"
    ],
    // For nodejs:
    // "lib": ["esnext"],
    // "types": ["node"],
    // and npm install -D @types/node
    // Other Outputs
    "sourceMap": true,
    "declaration": true,
    "declarationMap": true,
    // Stricter Typechecking Options
    "noUncheckedIndexedAccess": true,
    // Style Options
    "noImplicitReturns": true,
    "noImplicitOverride": true,
    "noUnusedLocals": true,
    "noUnusedParameters": true,
    "noFallthroughCasesInSwitch": true,
    // "noPropertyAccessFromIndexSignature": true,
    // Recommended Options
    "strict": true,
    "jsx": "react-jsx",
    "isolatedModules": true,
    "noUncheckedSideEffectImports": true,
    "moduleDetection": "force",
    "skipLibCheck": true,
    "lib": [
      "dom",
      "dom.iterable",
      "esnext"
    ],
    "allowJs": true,
    "noEmit": true,
    "incremental": true,
    "esModuleInterop": true,
    "moduleResolution": "bundler",
    "resolveJsonModule": true,
    "paths": {
      "@/*": [
        "./src/*"
      ]
    },
    "plugins": [
      {
        "name": "next"
      }
    ]
  },
  "include": [
    "next-env.d.ts",
    "**/*.mts",
    "**/*.ts",
    "**/*.tsx",
    ".next/types/**/*.ts",
    ".next/dev/types/**/*.ts"
  ],
  // `.next/types/**/*.ts` and `.next/dev/types/**/*.ts` are BACK, deliberately,
  // and this comment is the second half of a story whose first half was true
  // and is not any more.
  //
  // They were removed 2026-08-26 for a real, measured reason: with `.next/`
  // populated, `tsc --noEmit` type-checked Next's own generated
  // `.next/types/validator.ts` and failed with `Type 'Route' does not satisfy
  // the constraint 'never'` — two errors that existed nowhere else. `tsc -p`
  // with the globs = exit 2, without = exit 0, on identical source. Every
  // local session saw a red tree CI called green.
  //
  // Two things then changed, and neither was noticed because nothing checks a
  // comment. First, REMOVING THEM DOES NOT STICK: `next build` and `next dev`
  // rewrite this file and add both globs back (Next prints "We detected
  // TypeScript in your project and reconfigured your tsconfig.json"). So the
  // line above claiming they were "deliberately gone" described a state that
  // ended at the next build, and the canonical checkout sat permanently dirty
  // in a tracked config file nobody had edited. Second, on Next 16.3.4 the
  // offending file is no longer generated: the globs now pull in exactly
  // `.next/dev/types/routes.d.ts` and `.next/dev/types/root-params.d.ts`, and
  // both type-check clean.
  //
  // Measured 2026-09-04 on this tree: `npm run typecheck` WITH both globs and
  // a populated `.next/` = exit 0, 0 errors, 2 generated files in the program
  // (`tsc --listFiles | grep /.next/`). CI is unaffected either way — it runs
  // on a fresh checkout where `.next/` does not exist and both globs match
  // nothing.
  //
  // So they stay. Fighting the framework over a file it rewrites on every
  // build bought a permanently dirty tree and no coverage. If the validator
  // error ever returns, `next build` still catches it independently —
  // `next.config.mjs` sets `typescript.ignoreBuildErrors: false`.
  "exclude": [
    "node_modules",
    "archive",
    "scripts",
    "supabase/functions",
    ".next",
    // replay/fixtures/**/*.test.ts(x) are inert snapshots of a repair's own
    // regression test, copied verbatim from a historical commit — their
    // relative imports (e.g. '../qualifier-lifecycle') resolve only once
    // replay/runners/run.mjs overlays them into a worktree checked out at
    // that commit, not in place under replay/fixtures/. See replay/README.md.
    "replay/fixtures"
  ]
}
